  DataGrid resolves a row's properties reflectively in a few places
  (DataGridDataConnection.UpdateDataProperties, DataGridCollectionView.GetItemType,
  TypeHelper.GetPropertyOrIndexer). Compiled bindings already reference every
  property the grid displays, so trimming would keep them anyway — this makes
  that guarantee explicit rather than incidental, so adding a property to a row
  model cannot quietly break the grid in an AOT build.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="stingray-tex-gui">
    <namespace fullname="Stingray.Gui.ViewModels" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
  <assembly fullname="Stingray.Core">
    <type fullname="Stingray.Core.Optimization.SkippedTexture" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
